@startuml MCP Integration Workflow

!theme plain
title SABER MCP Integration - Current Implementation (Inspect AI + FastMCP)

actor Agent
participant "Inspect AI\n(mcp_server_http)" as InspectMCP
participant "SessionRestAPI\n(REST)" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI\n(FastMCP)" as MCP
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "MCPToolGenerator" as ToolGen

== Session Initialization (REST First) ==
Agent -> REST: POST /api/v1/session?client_id=client_id
REST -> SM: create_session(client_id)
SM -> REST: ClientSession
REST -> Agent: session_id

== Episode Creation (REST) ==
Agent -> REST: POST /api/v1/episode/{session_id}?task_id=task_id
REST -> SM: create_episode(session_id, task_id)
SM -> EM_EP: start_episode(session_id, task_id, task)
EM_EP -> SM: Episode
SM -> REST: EpisodeCreateResponse
REST -> Agent: episode_id

== MCP Connection via Inspect AI ==
Agent -> InspectMCP: mcp_server_http(url, headers)
note right: Inspect AI creates MCP connection with headers:\n- X-SABER-Session-ID: session_id\n- X-SABER-Episode-ID: episode_id\n- X-SABER-Task-ID: task_id\n- X-SABER-Orchestration-Env: INSPECT
InspectMCP -> MCP: HTTP connection with headers
MCP -> MCP: _get_headers()
note right: Parses headers using get_http_headers():\n- Validates orchestration_env (MANDATORY)\n- Extracts session context from headers\n- No session creation via MCP
MCP -> InspectMCP: connection established

== Tool Discovery (Dynamic Registration) ==
Agent -> InspectMCP: list_tools()
InspectMCP -> MCP: handle_list_tools()
MCP -> MCP: _get_headers()
note right: Extract orchestration_env and episode context
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: to_mcp_tools(episode_id)
EM_EXEC -> ToolGen: get_available_executors()
ToolGen -> EM_EXEC: dynamic_tool_schemas[]
note right of EM_EXEC: Returns clean tool schemas:\n- python(code: str)\n- cli(command: str)\n- end_episode(submission?: str) [STANDALONE only]
EM_EXEC -> MCP: executor_tools + conditional_hardcoded_tools
MCP -> InspectMCP: mcp.types.Tool[]
InspectMCP -> Agent: available_tools[]

== Command Execution (Header-Based Session Context) ==
Agent -> InspectMCP: python(code="print('hello')")
InspectMCP -> MCP: handle_call_tool("python", args)
MCP -> MCP: _get_headers()
note right: Session context retrieved from HTTP headers:\n- session_id, episode_id from headers\n- orchestration_env validation\n- No session_id in tool parameters
MCP -> MCP: _convert_to_action(tool_name, args)
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, episode_id, action)
SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action, headers)
EM_EXEC -> SM: CommandResult
SM -> EM_EP: step(session_id, action, result)
EM_EP -> SM: step_result
SM -> MCP: CommandResult
MCP -> MCP: _convert_to_mcp_result(CommandResult)
MCP -> InspectMCP: mcp.types.CallToolResult
InspectMCP -> Agent: command_result

== Episode End (Multiple Modes) ==

alt STANDALONE Orchestration
    Agent -> InspectMCP: end_episode(submission="flag{found}")
    InspectMCP -> MCP: _handle_end_episode_call(args)
    MCP -> MCP: _get_headers()
    MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, episode_id, result_action)
    note right: Records submission first
    MCP -> SM: end_episode(session_id, episode_id, "agent_completed", EvalSubmission)
    SM -> EM_EP: end_episode()
    EM_EP -> SM: episode_ended
    SM -> MCP: success
    MCP -> InspectMCP: submission_text
    InspectMCP -> Agent: episode_completed
else INSPECT Orchestration
    note right of Agent: Episode end handled by inspect_ai framework:\n- Agent execution completes naturally\n- EvalSubmission created from ModelOutput\n- Episode ended via REST API
    Agent -> REST: end_episode via agent completion
    REST -> SM: end_episode(session_id, episode_id, "agent_completed", EvalSubmission)
    SM -> EM_EP: end_episode()
    EM_EP -> SM: episode_ended
    SM -> REST: success
end

== Session Cleanup ==
Agent -> InspectMCP: disconnect()
InspectMCP -> MCP: connection_closed
Agent -> REST: DELETE /api/v1/session/{session_id} (optional)
REST -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
SM -> SM: cleanup_session_resources()

note right of MCP
**Current MCP Implementation - FastMCP Server**
✅ Clean tool schemas (no session_id in parameters)
✅ Header-based session mapping via get_http_headers()
✅ Pure functional tool interfaces
✅ Native inspect_ai mcp_server_http() compatibility
✅ HTTP transport with mandatory header validation

**Tool Schema Examples:**
- python(code: str)
- cli(command: str)
- end_episode(submission?: str) [STANDALONE mode only]

**Key Implementation Features:**
- FastMCP server with HTTP transport (/mcp endpoint)
- Mandatory X-SABER-Orchestration-Env header validation
- Dynamic tool registration via MCPToolGenerator
- Conditional hardcoded tools based on orchestration mode
- Direct inspect_ai integration without wrapper clients
end note

note right of REST
**SessionRestAPI Responsibilities - Current Implementation**
- Session lifecycle management (create/terminate)
- Episode management (create/end)
- Task configuration and policy retrieval
- Benchmark information and task listings
- Health checks with manifest metadata
- Evaluation operations (criteria, file upload, override)
- No SSE - replaced with direct HTTP endpoints
end note

note right of SM
**Dual Protocol Architecture - Current Implementation**
- REST API (FastAPI) for session/episode management and evaluation
- MCP API (FastMCP) for clean tool execution only
- Header-based session context mapping with orchestration environment validation
- Single ClientSessionManager using REST + native inspect_ai MCP integration
- No automatic session creation via MCP - sessions must exist before MCP use
- Multi-episode session support with cascade termination
- Comprehensive resource cleanup and health monitoring
end note

note right of InspectMCP
**Inspect AI MCP Integration - Current Implementation**
- Native mcp_server_http() integration - no SABER wrapper needed
- Session context passed automatically via HTTP headers
- Tool execution handled directly by inspect_ai framework
- Episode lifecycle managed by inspect_ai agent execution
- Clean separation: inspect_ai handles MCP protocol, SABER provides tools
- Fail-fast header validation ensures proper session mapping

**Orchestration Modes:**
- **INSPECT**: Full inspect_ai integration, episode end via agent completion
- **STANDALONE**: Direct tool usage, end_episode tool available
- Header validation ensures consistent behavior across modes
end note

@enduml
